HTML 

Interesting facts about HTML

.its not a programming language - its a markup language designed to structure and present content on the web
.its everywhere - besides web browsers, its also in many applications, email clients, and even mobile apps 
.its platform independent - it can run on any platform or browser, making it incredibly versatile and universally accessible 
.its case insensitive - lowercase is preferred for consistency
.no closing tags for some elements - self closing 
.semantic elements exist to improve content organization and accessibility 
.its still evolving 
.APIs - it supports several powerful APIs
    .geolocation API to access user location 
    .canvas API for drawing graphics and animations 
    .web storage for storing data locally in the browser 
.comments - can be added, always, anytime 
.custom elements - it allows developers to create their own custom tags using Web Components, providing flexibility and reusability
.as an Art - its used with CSS to create ASCII art or intricate designs, showcasing its creative potential beyond 
functionality


Interesting Facts about Links and Navigation 

.links (anchors) - they enable users to navigate between the different web pages or sections of the same page 

1. HTTP link Header for Resource Preloading 
    .servers can send a link header to preload resources before the HTML is parsed
        .this is different from the <link> tag; its used for advanced performance optimization
            link: </styles.css>; rel=preload; as=style

2. <base> tag for global URLs 
    .it sets a default URL for all relative links, simplifying navigation 
        <a href="about.adagga.com">About Adagga</a>

3. multi-recipient email links
    .create a link that sends an email to multiple recipients by separating their email addresses with a comma. can also include a subject line
        <a href="edgarorina@gmail.com, edgar.momanyi.1@us.af.mil?subject=Hello">Email Us</a>

4. link to specific page section
    .using the id attribute, create links that navigate to specific sections within the same page
        .particularly useful for long pages with multiple sections 

5. tooltip links with title 
    .adding a title attribute creates a tooltip when hovering over a link
        <a href="https://www.edgarorina.com/" title="Visit my homepage">Edgar Adagga</a>
        